\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Rafael Nadal's posterior ability path from 1{,}317 matches (top) and the law of its argmax (bottom). The path has two highs, at 2013 and 2018, and the argmax law puts $0.27$ and $0.22$ on them, with the seasons between them carrying almost no mass. The band in the top panel shows where the highs are. It does not give their probabilities, and no summary of the yearly marginals does either.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nadal}{{1}{6}{Rafael Nadal's posterior ability path from 1{,}317 matches (top) and the law of its argmax (bottom). The path has two highs, at 2013 and 2018, and the argmax law puts $0.27$ and $0.22$ on them, with the seasons between them carrying almost no mass. The band in the top panel shows where the highs are. It does not give their probabilities, and no summary of the yearly marginals does either}{figure.1}{}}
